> Actual generated note streams

The two saved sample files retain the original temperature and seed choices, shown in the complete program. These are reconstructed procedural pitch-class melodies; the plot does not claim recovery of the missing MIDI file roundtrip.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/midi_lstm_notes.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){auto load=[](const std::string&path){auto a=dm::nn::load_npz(path);return std::map<std::string,dm::nn::Tensor>(a.begin(),a.end());};auto layout=dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2);for(auto file:{"sample08.npz","sample12.npz"}){auto a=load("build/nn-completion/models/midi_lstm/"+std::string(file));auto note=a.at("notes").to_vector<double>();std::vector<double>x(note.size());std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),0.);auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();plot.points(x,note,"actual sampled pitch class",{37,99,235},5).ylim(-.5,11.5).x_label("Generated note index").y_label("Pitch class0..11").title(file);layout.add(plot);}layout.size(1200,550).fit_panels().save_svg("build/midi_lstm_notes.svg");}
